    <h3>Getting all Shiny Pokémon in Black 2</h3>
    <p>
      Most Pokémon can be shiny simply by being lucky when encountering them. However, some Pokémon encounters or gifts are programmed to never be shiny. The following lists the Pokémon that requires a specific way to get them so they are shiny.
    </p>
    
    <ul>
      <li>Mew: Japanese Emerald (Old Sea Map event).</li>
      <li>Deoxys: English Emerald, FireRed, LeafGreen (AuroraTicket event)</li>
      <li>Manaphy: Trade from Pokémon Ranger to Pokémon Diamond/Pearl to Black 2, which obtained it from mission Recover the Precious Egg! unlocked with password P8M2-9D6F-43H7. You must trade the egg to another player with a different Trainer ID and Secret ID, then hatch it there (otherwise it can't be shiny).</li>
      <li>Darkrai: Platinum (requires Member Card)</li>
      <li>Shaymin: Platinum (requires Oak's Letter)</li>
      <li>Tornadus: Black (Tornadus from Dream Radar can't be shiny.)</li>
      <li>Thundurus: White (Thundurus from Dream Radar can't be shiny.)</li>
      <li>Genesect: Event Movie 2013 Genesect (Japan). For non-shiny: The Plasma Genesect on October 12, 2012.</li>
      <li>Celebi: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Arceus: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Victini: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Reshiram: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Zekrom: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Keldeo: Impossible to get shiny</li>
      <li>Meloetta: Impossible to get shiny</li>
    </ul>

